// src/std/core/loop/loop.zen
// the loop family's surface: nothing but starred re-exports.
//
// A folder root is a file of starred bindings and nothing else -
// that is what makes folders work, and it is why the family can be
// four files instead of one long one without anyone importing
// `std.core.loop.loop_iter` by hand. The prefix earned the folder:
// three files sharing a `loop_` prefix inside `core/` would have no
// root, so every consumer would import the pieces and every move
// inside the family would break them.
//
// Range travels with the family because it is the family's
// parameter type, the same way str and String travel together:
// every signature in loop_iter.zen names it, and a `loop` you
// cannot hand a Range to is not the export anyone wanted. It is
// DECLARED in std.core.range, which is the module that answers
// "what is iterable", not "what is a loop" - std.collections uses
// it as a plain index interval without ever calling a loop word.

Range*               = std.core.range
LoopHandle*          = std.core.loop.loop_handle
loop*, pairs*        = std.core.loop.loop_iter
find*, filter*, map* = std.core.loop.loop_find
